      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:5:2:9",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ مَنْ أَخْرَجَ زَكَاةَ مَالِهِ تَامَّةً فَوَضَعَهَا فِي مَوْضِعِهَا لَمْ يُسْأَلْ مِنْ أَيْنَ اكْتَسَبَ مَالَهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Fazzal, from Ali Bin Uqba, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Al Hassan<sup>asws</sup>, meaning the 1<sup>st</sup>, said, ‘I heard him<sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘The one who takes out the complete <span class=\"iTxt\">Zakāt</span> of his wealth, so he places it in its (appropriate) place, would not be asked (on the Day of Judgement) from where he earned his wealth’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "9. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn Faddal from Ali ibn ‘Uqbah from abu al-Hassan, the first, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, who has said the following: “If one pays, completely, the amount of zakat which is due on his wealth to the proper recipient, he is not asked how he has earned his wealth.” "
        ]
      }
    },
